"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":9062,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":983,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":9062,"open_issues":983,"watchers":53172,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/pulls/9750","html_url":"https://github.com/vuejs/core/pull/9750","diff_url":"https://github.com/vuejs/core/pull/9750.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/vuejs/core/pull/9750.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"fix #9742 \r\n\r\nWhen user add a proxy to a reactive array and use motheds of Array such as `push/pop/shift/unshift/includes/indexOf/lastIndexOf/splice`, the result of `toRaw(proxy)` will always return proxy and infinitely trigger `toRaw` because `receiver` isn't the origin proxy(created by vue) of `target`.\r\n\r\nSo I think when we use the above methods, it should skip the comparsion between `receiver` and the origin proxy(created by vue) of `target`.\r\n\r\n```js\r\n// Create a reactive array\r\nconst originalArray = reactive([]);\r\n\r\n// Create a Proxy around the reactive array\r\nconst proxyArray = new Proxy(originalArray, {});\r\n\r\n// Pushing elements to the Proxy array\r\nproxyArray.push(1); // this will trigger toRaw infinitely\r\n```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/9750/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/9750/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"pikax","i